1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,700
Media Studio: a fictional record release, made and published with real software.

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:08,700
Setup starts with Node 24 or newer, Docker and a Workers Paid account; the official trial proves the host locally.

3
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:13,700
Deploy the standalone Oyster host with --minify. The unminified bundle exceeded the worker startup limit on this account.

4
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:18,700
Do not install all seven starter apps. Pack the pinned Prints commit and install only that release, plus the desktop.

5
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:23,700
In Composer, enable Images and video. It checks the host catalogue without generating or buying anything.

6
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:48,233
The article leads with the actual sleeve and a release table you can inspect object by object.

7
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:56,700
The host runs Oyster with Prints installed — the desktop is optional, the native controls are the product.

8
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:10,700
The studio opens with the existing owner sign-in; the library and publishing controls are native to the studio.

9
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:14,700
Creating a still shows the model, the reference and the estimate before anything is sent.

10
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:25,500
The request records its intent first, so a lost reply never becomes a silent charge.

11
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:29,500
Each saved result keeps its prompt, model, settings and provenance. Prompts stay private.

12
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:39,167
The asset view offers download, publication and the separate show-or-hide placement control.

13
00:01:39,767 --> 00:01:51,167
Signed out, the published clip plays from owned storage with no owner passphrase.

14
00:01:51,767 --> 00:01:56,167
Pausing stops new work; the Computer sleeps after fifteen idle minutes; reopening reads the saved bytes without regenerating.

15
00:01:56,767 --> 00:02:00,167
Public downloads are deliberate derivatives; generated masters and receipts stay in the private project.

16
00:02:00,767 --> 00:02:08,833
Every public download carries the fictional-release note and a stable address.

17
00:02:09,433 --> 00:02:16,267
The tutorial records the real path, including the billing gate and the startup limit.

18
00:02:16,867 --> 00:02:23,267
The same article at 390 pixels, with no horizontal overflow.

19
00:02:23,867 --> 00:02:27,267
Made in the studio we built. The application is the lasting product.
